{#
  The plain-text half of an account-security email: a password reset, an account
  activation.

  Two differences from `notification.v1`, and both are the reason this is a
  separate template rather than a flag on that one:

  * **No link, and `action_url` is never read here.** A message about somebody's
    password that asks them to click something is the exact shape of a phishing
    email, and training the platform's users to follow one is a cost that
    outlasts the convenience. The reader signs in the way they always do.
  * **It ends with `security_note`** — "if you did not do this, contact your
    administrator" — which is the only thing that makes an unexpected password
    reset actionable rather than alarming.
#}
{{ chrome.greeting }}

{{ title }}

{{ message }}

{{ chrome.security_note }}

--
{{ platform_name }}
{{ chrome.footer }}
{{ chrome.no_reply }}
